Z||000008||Songman||10-10-2000||01:14 PM||||I've had 3 911s. One coupe and two Targas. If you go back into the early 70s the cars are actually pretty reasonable. From 74 to 86 the cars were identical to look at. You can get a good running 74 for about $7k if you look around. And don't believe all those astronomical maintenance numbers either. You don't have to adjust the valves every six months like they say. Just regular stuff is all that is needed. Take it to the dealer or a garage and they will nail you. Do it yourself and you'll be just fine!<P>Only one thing - Don't do what I did. I was going to build myself a performance 911! Those headers sure looked and sounded good.. Right up to the time I drove it to Ohio in the winter to see one of my old girlfriends! Who would have ever thought that the heat came from the exhaust! heheh||||reg||1
